<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). It is the note of the Linux one: Breeze's
     audio-x-generic, the packaging/warptempo_gui.desktop's Icon=, vendored
     verbatim as assets/icons/breeze/audio-x-generic.svg (the 64 px mimetype
     rendition), with its disc dropped and its note alone centred on the
     platter (architect 2026-09-30, on his glass look: "the logo is off
     center. Better to just remove the little CD finger tab altogether and
     center the icon"; the whole file rendered at fit stood one evening,
     2026-09-29). An ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so no
     legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  solid opaque #aaaaaa, the sheet's own fill
                                   in the Breeze file (fill="#aaa"): the
                                   platter IS the sheet, its edges gone;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the note, RGBA, white at the file's .75
                                   opacity (so it lands #eaeaea over the grey,
                                   as the Breeze glyph paints it), on a
                                   transparent surround.
     Nothing else of the file is drawn: no disc, no sheet outline, no top or
     bottom line, no gradient.

     THE 44-OF-72 RULE. Every mask (circle, squircle, rounded square: the
     launcher's choice) is drawn within the central 72 dp viewport of the
     108 dp canvas; the note's bounding box is 44 dp tall there, the ordinary
     launcher-glyph proportion, and centred on the canvas. The box, measured
     by rendering the note path alone and trimming it, is x 15..37,
     y 24.994..46.997 in the file's coordinates (before its group's
     translate): 22 by 22.003 units, so the width at 44 dp tall rounds to
     44 dp at every density and the box is square.

     THE DERIVED SVG. The recipe's input is android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg,
     beside the manifest and outside res/ (aapt2 compiles res/ whole and
     refuses an unknown file there): one path whose d is copied byte for byte
     from the vendored file (a diff between the two d strings is a
     transcription bug), fill #fff, opacity .75, in a viewBox that is the
     note's box, so the file renders the note edge to edge.

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop and
     committed; a retouch is a re-run of this recipe, never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). The recipe, from the repo root
     (rsvg-convert 2.62, ImageMagick 7), for each density n at factor f
     (mdpi 1, hdpi 1.5, xhdpi 2, xxhdpi 3, xxxhdpi 4) with C = 108·f,
     H = 44·f, W = H (the box's aspect, rounded to whole pixels) and the
     page offset O = (C − H) / 2 = 32·f on both axes:

       mdpi     C=108 H=W=44  O=32      hdpi    C=162 H=W=66  O=48
       xhdpi    C=216 H=W=88  O=64      xxhdpi  C=324 H=W=132 O=96
       xxxhdpi  C=432 H=W=176 O=128

       rsvg-convert -w W -h H \
           - -page-width C - -page-height C - -left O - -top O \
           android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg -o fg.png
       magick fg.png -strip -define png:compression-level=9 \
           -define png:compression-filter=5 \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_foreground.png
       magick -size CxC xc:'#aaaaaa' -strip \
           PNG8:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_background.png

     (The long options are spelt "- -" above only because an XML comment may
     not hold two adjacent hyphens: type them as the usual double hyphen.)
     The foreground stays RGBA: a palette encoding of it is not lossless (its
     antialiased alpha edges), while the one-colour background is. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
